      "strategyPlan": "Focus on capitalizing on the anticipated growth in stablecoin adoption by (1) closely tracking the Circle partnership announcements and increasing USDC usage, (2) evaluating the upcoming Arc Layer‑1 blockchain for potential investment or integration opportunities, and (3) incorporating the new risk‑screening tools into portfolio risk management to stay ahead of compliance shifts. Maintain a diversified stablecoin allocation, favor those with clear regulatory backing, and set alerts for regulatory or technological developments that could shift market sentiment.",
      "riskAnalysis": "Key risks include regulatory tightening as compliance‑focused risk‑assessment tools become standard; technological risk from the launch of a new blockchain dedicated to stablecoin finance, which may face adoption hurdles; and market risk stemming from rapid shifts in stablecoin demand driven by partnership news. Additionally, liquidity risk remains elevated for smaller stablecoins, and counterparty risk persists with issuers like Circle. Overreliance on a single stablecoin or platform can amplify losses if adverse news materializes.",
